Feature acceptance specification
Lesson attendance
Teacher selects class, subject, date and lesson number; enrolled learner list is loaded from the school's learner records.
Per learner status: Present, Absent, Late, Excused.
Save records against school, teacher, class, subject, date and lesson.
Summary filters: class, subject, teacher and date range; show counts and attendance percentages.
Corrections are permission-controlled and auditable.
Records of work
Choose grade/subject and curriculum design; suggest strand, sub-strand, topic, outcomes and learning experiences.
Save date taught, planned/taught lesson count, and remarks/challenges.
Curriculum suggestions show source and verification state.
Teacher-selected content
Allow selecting strand/sub-strand and adding a custom topic/lesson.
Set entry_source = teacher-entered and curriculum source teacher-entered.
Never label custom entries as official curriculum content.
Shared data / TPAD
Lesson attendance and records of work are the source records; summaries and TPAD evidence should reference them rather than re-enter the same data.
TPAD preparation can select records by teacher, date range, class and subject, then attach or cite evidence.
Appraisal evidence export should include record date, lesson details, reflection and evidence links.
School boundaries
Every record has a school_id. Staff access must be checked against the JengaEdu school membership/role system.
Teachers create/edit their own entries; heads/authorized administrators can view school-wide summaries.
Test tenant isolation before enabling shared staff access.
